    ("In an election between two candidates, the winner gets 65% of total votes and wins by a margin of 900 votes. How many total votes were cast?", "3,000 votes. Winner = 65%, Loser = 35%. Difference = 30%. 30% of total votes = 900 -> Total votes = 900 / 0.30 = 3,000.", "Easy", "Problem Solving", "", "What if there were invalid votes?"),
    ("A student scores 36% marks and fails by 32 marks. Another student scores 48% marks and gets 64 marks more than the pass mark. What is the maximum mark?", "800 marks. Difference in percentage = 48% - 36% = 12%. Difference in marks = 64 - (-32) = 96 marks. 12% = 96 -> 100% = (96 / 12) * 100 = 800 marks.", "Intermediate", "Problem Solving", "", "What is the pass mark percentage?"),
    ("What is 15% of 240 plus 25% of 160?", "76. 15% of 240 = 0.15 * 240 = 36. 25% of 160 = 160 / 4 = 40. Total = 36 + 40 = 76.", "Easy", "Problem Solving", "", "What is 25% written as a fraction?"),
    ("If 60% of students in a class of 50 are boys, how many girls are in the class?", "20 girls. Boys = 60% of 50 = 30 boys. Girls = 50 - 30 = 20 girls (or 40% of 50 = 20).", "Easy", "Problem Solving", "", "What is the ratio of boys to girls?"),
    ("A man spends 70% of his income. If his income increases by 20% and his expenditure increases by 10%, what is the percentage increase in his savings?", "43.33%. Let income = 100, expense = 70, savings = 30. New income = 120, new expense = 70 * 1.10 = 77. New savings = 120 - 77 = 43. Increase = (13 / 30) * 100 = 43.33%.", "Intermediate", "Problem Solving", "", "What is savings formula?"),
