    ("Percentages MCQ: A fruit vendor sells 40% of his apples and still has 420 apples left. How many apples did he have originally?", "Option C is correct. 60% left = 420 -> Total = 420 / 0.60 = 700 apples.", "Easy", "MCQ", "", {"A": "588", "B": "600", "C": "700", "D": "720"}, "C", "How many did he sell?"),
    ("Percentages MCQ: By what percentage is 80 greater than 50?", "Option A is correct. Increase = (80 - 50)/50 * 100 = 30/50 * 100 = 60%.", "Easy", "MCQ", "", {"A": "60%", "B": "30%", "C": "37.5%", "D": "50%"}, "A", "By what percentage is 50 less than 80?"),
    ("Percentages MCQ: If x is 20% less than y, then y is what percentage more than x?", "Option C is correct. y = 100, x = 80. Difference = 20. % more = (20/80) * 100 = 25%.", "Easy", "MCQ", "", {"A": "20%", "B": "22.5%", "C": "25%", "D": "30%"}, "C", "Why is it not 20%?"),
    ("If salary of X is 25% more than Y, then by what percent is Y's salary less than X?", "20%. Let Y = 100, X = 125. Difference = 25. Percent less = (25 / 125) * 100 = 20%.", "Easy", "Problem Solving", "", "What if X is 50% more than Y?"),
    ("What single discount is equivalent to two successive discounts of 20% and 10%?", "28%. Single equivalent discount = d1 + d2 - (d1*d2)/100 = 20 + 10 - 2 = 28%. If price = 100: 100 -> 80 -> 72 (28% off).", "Easy", "Problem Solving", "", "What about 20% and 20%?"),
    ("A mixture contains 80% milk and 20% water. In 50 liters of this mixture, how much water must be added to make water 50%?", "30 liters. In 50L: Milk = 40L, Water = 10L. To make water 50%, water must equal milk (40L). Water to add = 40L - 10L = 30 liters.", "Intermediate", "Problem Solving", "", "What is the new total volume?"),
    ("In an examination, 70% candidates passed in English and 80% passed in Math, while 10% failed in both. If 144 candidates passed in both, what is the total number of candidates?", "240 candidates. Failed in both = 10% -> Passed in at least one = 90%. Passed both = 70% + 80% - 90% = 60%. 60% = 144 -> Total = 144 / 0.60 = 240.", "Intermediate", "Problem Solving", "", "How many failed in English?"),
    ("If the side of a square is increased by 30%, what is the percentage increase in its area?", "69%. Area = s^2. Increase% = 30 + 30 + (30*30/100) = 60 + 9 = 69%.", "Easy", "Problem Solving", "", "What if side is decreased by 10%?"),
    ("Due to a 20% reduction in the price of wheat, a man can buy 5 kg more for $100. What was the original price per kg?", "$5 per kg. Money saved = 20% of 100 = $20. This buys 5kg, so reduced price = 20 / 5 = $4/kg. Reduced price is 80% of original: 0.8 * original = 4 -> Original = $5/kg.", "Intermediate", "Problem Solving", "", "What is the reduced price per kg?"),

