    ("Profit Loss MCQ: If an item is sold at 20% loss for $480, what was its cost price?", "Option C is correct. 0.8 * CP = 480 -> CP = 480 / 0.8 = $600.", "Easy", "MCQ", "", {"A": "$500", "B": "$576", "C": "$600", "D": "$620"}, "C", "What would be 10% profit SP?"),
    ("Profit Loss MCQ: When SP of two items is identical with equal profit% and loss% of 20%, what is the net result?", "Option A is correct. Always a loss of (20/10)^2 = 4% loss.", "Easy", "MCQ", "", {"A": "4% loss", "B": "No profit no loss", "C": "2% profit", "D": "4% profit"}, "A", "Does selling price value matter?"),
    ("Profit Loss MCQ: An article is marked at $120 and sold for $102. What is the discount rate?", "Option D is correct. Discount = 18. Discount% = (18/120) * 100 = 15%.", "Easy", "MCQ", "", {"A": "10%", "B": "12%", "C": "18%", "D": "15%"}, "D", "What is the marked price?"),
    ("A vendor bought bananas at 6 for $10 and sold them at 4 for $8. What is his profit or loss percentage?", "20% profit. CP per banana = 10/6 = $1.667. SP per banana = 8/4 = $2.00. Profit per banana = 2 - 1.667 = $0.333. Profit% = (0.333 / 1.667) * 100 = 20%.", "Intermediate", "Problem Solving", "", "How many bananas to make $10 profit?"),
    ("A trader marks his goods so as to make 20% profit after allowing a discount of 10%. If CP is $300, what is the marked price?", "$400. Required SP = 300 * 1.20 = $360. MP after 10% discount gives SP: 0.9 * MP = 360 -> MP = 360 / 0.9 = $400.", "Intermediate", "Problem Solving", "", "What is the discount amount in dollars?"),
    ("If selling price is doubled, the profit triples. What is the original profit percentage?", "100%. Let CP = C, SP = S. Profit P = S - C. New SP = 2S, new profit = 2S - C = 3P. Substitute: 2S - C = 3(S - C) -> 2S - C = 3S - 3C -> S = 2C. Original profit = S - C = 2C - C = C. Profit% = (C/C) * 100 = 100%.", "Intermediate", "Problem Solving", "", "What is SP in terms of CP?"),
